rt of our work up for treatment to  make sure they don't have a co-infection  but it's not very common  all right thank you  and it looks like we have time for one  more question  what about a combo hcv assay antibody  plus antigen like we have for hiv would  it be useful  yeah again it kind of goes to what i was  saying before i think it's useful in  certain settings so i think it could be  useful if um the cost is reasonable for  that setting and if it makes sense to do  the screening test at all so in the  context of hiv it's a little bit  different because of course an antibody  positivity is indicative of infection  and so even though we do this in our  fourth generation hiv assay so antibody  testing plus antigen testing we're  really looking for infection there in  the context of hep c it could have  utility for screening but if we already  know people are antibody positive which  i mean at least where i let where i am  in the world people are tested sometimes  five times for any body positivity um it  might not be that helpful so i think it  does really depend on the intention of  the test and this ability to mix and  match i just can't emphasize that enough  because it's not going to be a one size  fits all for this population  all right thank you thank you dr biandi  do you have any final comments for our  audience  i just wanted to again say thank you for  joining me today um in the context of  world hepatitis and really thinking  about elimination um you know this is  really grassroots work this is really  working within your community with  working within your network and then  getting that political advocacy and  engagement so you've taken the first  step by coming and attending here today  and please feel free to reach out to me  for any additional questions and follow  up  thank you again dr biandi for your time  today and your important research  we would also like to thank lab roots  and our sponsor abbott diagnostics for  underwriting today's educational webcast  before we go i'd like to thank the  audience for joining us today and for  their interesting questions  questions we did not have time for today  and those submitted during the on-demand  period will be addressed by the speaker  via the contact information you provided  at the time of registration  this webcast can be viewed on demand  lab routes will alert you via email when  it's available for replay we encourage  you to share that email with your  colleagues who may have missed today's  live event  until next time take care everyone and  goodbye  you

